notes               = "Titled in source (شب یلدا... هجرانی..., printed above the poem). Yalda is the winter solstice, the longest night of the year and traditionally one spent awake in company; a hejrâni Yalda is therefore the longest night of the year spent apart, which is the whole poem. The close makes a duet of the ghazal's two states — وصل می‌زد، هجران می‌خواند: union plays the instrument, parting sings. زمستان ۱۳۶۸ is winter, so the Gregorian half is 1990 (+622). Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
